# Citation metadata, in the Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# GitHub reads this file and offers a "Cite this repository" button from it.
#
# Two fields are deliberately absent until they exist, rather than carrying a
# placeholder that could be cited by mistake:
#
#   doi             once the software is deposited and given one
#   date-released   once there is a release to date
#
# A `preferred-citation` block belongs here too once the BioHackathon 2026
# preprint has a DOI, so that citing the software cites the paper instead.
#
# The format has no field for a ROR id, so the affiliations here are the
# free-text names only. The RORs live in the preprint's front matter, which
# does have a field for them.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: iyo
abstract: >-
  A publishing tool for OWL, RDFS, SKOS and SHACL vocabularies. It writes a
  themeable website with one page per term, each term also available as
  Markdown, Turtle and JSON-LD, and context files for AI agents alongside the
  human-readable documentation. It also writes a manifest describing the content
  negotiation the site needs, compiles that manifest into configuration for
  several hosts, and can check a live deployment against it.
type: software
authors:
